<%# UI Dialog — self-contained trigger + modal: the trigger, the open state
    and the backdrop ship as one fragment, so state never crosses a partial
    boundary. Esc / outside clicks close via event-qualified set (the lab
    palette shape). The whole overlay flips through a presence binding
    (hidden = !shown), NOT a branch arm — arms inside a partial are never
    materialized in 0.6.0. The body is a `content:` local: render-with-block
    inside a partial breaks the slots re-render (TypeError, 0.6.0 measured).
    locals: cta:, label:, content: %>
<%# herb:state (shown: false) %>
<button class="ui-btn ui-btn-primary" data-herb-set="shown=true"><%= cta %></button>
<div class="ui-dialog-backdrop" hidden="<%= !shown %>">
  <div class="ui-dialog" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="<%= label %>" data-herb-set="click@outside->shown=false keydown.esc@window->shown=false">
    <p class="ui-dialog-body"><%= content %></p>
    <div class="ui-dialog-actions">
      <button class="ui-btn ui-btn-ghost" data-herb-reset="shown">閉じる</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
